# Netlify / Cloudflare Pages redirect rules.
#
# Every tool moved from a category-prefixed path to a flat root slug
# (/tools/json-formatter -> /json-formatter). These 301s are what consolidate the
# old URLs' link equity onto the new ones; the in-app <LegacyToolRedirect> is only
# a fallback for hosts that do not read this file, and a client-side redirect is a
# materially weaker signal than a real 301.
#
# First match wins, so the per-tool rules below sit above the catch-all. Category
# listing pages (/pdf-tools) are untouched because these patterns all require a
# second path segment.

/tools/*                 /:splat   301!
/pdf-tools/*             /:splat   301!
/csv-tools/*             /:splat   301!
/audio-tools/*           /:splat   301!
/image-tools/*           /:splat   301!
/video-tools/*           /:splat   301!
/spreadsheet-tools/*     /:splat   301!
/compression-tools/*     /:splat   301!
/archive-tools/*         /:splat   301!
/converter-tools/*       /:splat   301!

# Every real route is prerendered to its own index.html, so anything left over is
# genuinely missing. Serving 404.html with a 404 status avoids the soft-404s that
# the usual SPA `/* /index.html 200` fallback produces.
/*                       /404.html 404
